plugging in a second controller to make  your character run faster sounds like  the setup for a bad video game meme  however that's exactly how some players  have discovered you can do so in Pokemon  scarlet and violet even though the setup  is a bit more complex than viral social  media posts will have you believe as one  popular tweet shows yes it is true that  you can double your character's run  speed in scarlet and violet by pressing  forward onto controllers at once however  your switch must be undocked and you  have to use a joy-con attached to the  switch along with a wireless controller  the game apparently confuses the  attached joy-con and the wireless  controller which allows both controllers  to provide input to the character  simultaneously as one reply to the  original post shows this doubled input  allows the joystick to go beyond its  normal range thus significantly  increasing the speed of your character  we were able to get this trick to work  in our own testing though it doesn't  work if you go directly backwards or  directly forwards which makes navigation  a little bit more annoying than usual  this Speed Run worthy exploit is just  one of many issues that Pokemon fans  have reported with scarlet and violet  another exploration glitch making its  way around the internet is one that  allows you to get up slopes that are  impeding your progress a clip posted to  Twitter by Zully the witch shows her  attempting to jump up a slope and  sliding down then she turns around and  leaps up the hill backwards successfully  making it up and if you're interested in  trying it yourself the key is to mash  the jump button as you descend once you  get a little bit further into the game  and get abilities like Glide and climb  the trick might be a little harder to  pull off however with those additional  movement tools you probably won't need  it as much while this latest entry in  the series has garnered positive review  scores this open world Pokemon  experience is marred by significant  technical flaws including low frame  rates visual glitches and frequent  stuttering however our critic jig Decker  still enjoyed the experience in our  Gamespot review of the games I am also  having a pretty great time even though  the stuttering makes my eyes hurt in  other Nintendo related news the Mario  Kart 8 Deluxe Booster course pass will  soon be halfway to the Finish Line as  the third wave of six has been confirmed  for a December 7th launch date Wave 3 of  the booster course pass will like the  previous waves add 8 more courses to  Mario Kart 8's roster with all of them  coming from previous games in the  franchise there's we Maple Tree Way from  Mario Kart Wii DS Peach Gardens for  Mario Kart DS and 3DS rainbow road from  Mario Kart 7 just to name a few Wave 3  comes over four months after the release  of the previous wave which brought the  turnip cup and propeller Cub on August  4th the booster course pass is available  as a separate purchase for 25 and it's  also included in the Nintendo switch  online plus expansion pass subscription  along with access to classic games from  the Sega Genesis and N64 days hit the  comment section let me know who you  picked as your starter in scarlet and  violet and we'll see you in the next one
 

